Consider the figure where $m\angle A = 34^{\circ}$, $m\angle B = 80^\circ$, and $m\angle C = 24^{\circ}$. What is the value of $x + y$, given that $x$ and $y$ are the measures of the angles as shown in a pentagon and an adjacent triangle respectively? Assume all intersections create vertical angles at joints and right angles where indicated. [asy]
