Since $e > 1$, we use the second part of the given piecewise function, $f(x) = f(\ln x)$ for $x \geqslant 1$.

Step 1: Find $f(e)$:
\begin{align*}
f(e) &= f(\ln e) & \text{(since $e = \ln e$)}\\
&= f(1) & \text{(as $\ln e = 1$)}\\
&= f(\ln 1) & \text{(using $f(x) = f(\ln x)$ for $x \geqslant 1$)}\\
&= f(0) & \text{(since $\ln 1 = 0$)}
\end{align*}

Step 2: Find $f(0)$ using $f(x) = e^{x} + 1$ for $x < 1$:
\begin{align*}
f(0) &= e^{0} + 1\\
&= 1 + 1\\
&= 2
\end{align*}

Therefore, $\boxed{f(e) = 2}$.

